# Retail data (port/docs/retail-eu-plan.md, R3): the merchant marks of the map with the European discs.
# The European map layout (SS/<lang>/ss_map.dat sub-file 6, IDC_SSCRN_0) has an eighth merchant mark,
# unit 0xB with its "H": the castle merchant after he moved (SCF_R204_MERCHANT_MOVE). The European
# Sscrn.rel shows marks 0..7 (getMerchantMarkNo 7 -> 0xB, markMerchantDisp eight) and in area 2 hides mark
# 2 once the merchant moved and mark 7 before (markMerchantPosition; its GLOBAL_WK has Scenario_flg 0xC
# further on). This build never placed or hid unit 0xB: an "H" stood in the middle of the map and stayed
# there while the map moved (device video, 27.10.2026). Nothing changes with the debug build's discs. A
# port patch for retail data.
# US release (port/docs/retail-us-plan.md): its Sscrn.rel merchant marks are the European code
# (markMerchantDisp, getMerchantMarkNo alike): both retail releases (re4_disc_retail).
--- a/src/Sscrn/ss_map.cpp
+++ b/src/Sscrn/ss_map.cpp
@@ -750,6 +750,12 @@
 
 // Merchant mark `no` of the area: stage 1 picks the parts by the stage flags, the others use the
 // parts in order.
+/* port: the European map has an eighth merchant mark (ss_map.dat sub-file 6 unit 0xB with its "H"):
+   the castle merchant after he moved (SCF_R204_MERCHANT_MOVE). The European Sscrn.rel shows marks
+   0..7 (getMerchantMarkNo 7 -> 0xB) and in area 2 hides mark 2 once he moved, mark 7 before.
+   Unplaced, unit 0xB stood in the middle of the map (device video, 27.10.2026). */
+extern "C" int re4_disc_retail(void); /* port: runtime/dvd.cpp */
+
 int markMerchantPosition(SUB_SCREEN* wk, int no, Vec* pos)
 {
     int st1a[2] = {0x22, 0};
